=begin
  libeo: the shared library for the e-scripts (ebounty, eloot, eherbs, ecleanse, eohunter, ...).

  Loaded once per session with Script.loadlib('libeo'); definitions persist after the
  library script exits. A script names the version it was built against and the library
  refuses a mismatch loudly:

    Script.loadlib('libeo')
    EO.require('0.3.0')

  This file only loads the library. The library itself is scripts/eo/, one file per
  concern (EO::Settings, EO::Containers, EO::Guild, EO::Herbs, ...); each file opens
  with what it holds, and README.md has the list.

  What lives here is script-side glue that Lich itself should not carry. Anything that
  is a game rule or parser plumbing belongs in Lich itself (Stance, Stash.wield, Bank,
  Mana.pulse, issue_command, Spell state, the Bounty parser) and is called directly; a
  script that needs it raises its required Lich version.

        author: elanthia-online
  contributors: Nisugi
          game: Gemstone
          tags: library, utility, eo
      required: Lich >= 5.22.0
       version: 0.3.0

  Version Control:
  Major_change.feature_addition.bugfix
  v0.3.0 (2026-11-12)
    - EO::Settings::ListForm: the ListSettingsForm window ebounty and eloot share (values to
      and from the window, the Add/Delete lists, the controls); each script keeps its tabs
    - EO::Settings: the setup window check, the settings table (get_category, get_setting,
      fill_defaults, prune), the profile file and the ListSettingsForm helpers, from the e-scripts
    - EO.say, EO.word_wrap: the e-scripts' message and wrap (the Lich check and the
      script version are Lich's own: Script.require_lich_version!, Script.version)
    - whether wounds allow a cast is Lich's Injured.able_to_cast? everywhere
    - EO::Containers asks Lich's Inventory about a carried container: OPEN only when it
      is closed, contents without LOOK IN; LOOK IN stays for the disk, a box on the
      floor, and a session without the extended feed
    - EO::Hands uses Lich's Stash for which hand holds what, and to open the way to
      an item in a closed container before taking it
  v0.2.0 (2026-11-11)
    - split into scripts/eo/, one file per concern, shipped by the eohunter gem
    - EO.room_id, EO.command / EO.result / EO.settle, EO::Containers.open
    - EO::Guild: ebounty's task logic (tables, NPCs, the taskmaster finder,
      location resolution, herb lookup); the guild dialogue (get, turn in,
      remove, expedite, the assignment NPCs, the guards) with TaskPolicy
  v0.1.0 (2026-09-10)
    - initial: EO.require / EO.version, EO.go2 / EO.at? / EO.nearest / EO.visit,
      EO.help
=end

base = File.join(SCRIPT_DIR, 'eo')
verbose = $VERBOSE
begin
  $VERBOSE = nil
  %w[version help messages settings travel command containers hands town items locker skinning appraisal loot selling locksmith hoard casting wander
     cleanse/tables cleanse/hazards cleanse/afflictions cleanse/disarms cleanse/traps
     coordination/protocol coordination/discovery coordination/parser_projection
     guild/tables guild/policy guild/npcs guild/location guild/forage
     guild/taskmaster guild/assignments guild/guards guild/completion
     guild/heirloom guild/escort_routes guild/escort guild/disablers guild/rescue
     herbs/table herbs/injuries herbs/doses herbs/sack herbs/heal herbs/shop].each do |part|
    load File.join(base, "#{part}.rb")
  end
ensure
  $VERBOSE = verbose
end
